---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { DONATE_URL } from "../lib/links";

const pageTitle = "How it works";
---

<style>
  .cnf-how {
    max-width: 720px;
  }

  .cnf-how ul {
    list-style-type: disc;
    padding-left: 1.5rem;
  }

  .cnf-how li + li {
    margin-top: 0.5rem;
  }

  /* FAQ: native <details>, so answers open without JS and find-in-page still
     reaches closed ones. */
  .cnf-how__faq {
    margin-top: 1rem;
    border-top: 1px solid hsla(var(--color-green), 0.2);
  }

  .cnf-how__question {
    border-bottom: 1px solid hsla(var(--color-green), 0.2);
  }

  .cnf-how__question summary {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 1rem;
    padding: 1rem 0;
    color: hsl(var(--color-green));
    font-family: "Playfair Display", serif;
    font-size: 1.25rem;
    cursor: pointer;
    list-style: none;
  }

  .cnf-how__question summary::-webkit-details-marker {
    display: none;
  }

  /* Same chevron as the nav's Explore menu. */
  .cnf-how__question summary::after {
    content: "";
    flex-shrink: 0;
    width: 0.5em;
    height: 0.5em;
    border-right: 1.5px solid currentColor;
    border-bottom: 1.5px solid currentColor;
    transform: translateY(-0.15em) rotate(45deg);
    transition: transform 0.2s ease;
  }

  .cnf-how__question[open] summary::after {
    transform: translateY(0.1em) rotate(-135deg);
  }

  .cnf-how__question summary:focus-visible {
    outline: 2px solid hsl(var(--color-green));
    outline-offset: 2px;
    border-radius: 4px;
  }

  .cnf-how__question p {
    margin: 0 0 1rem;
  }
</style>

<BaseLayout
  pageTitle={pageTitle}
  description="How Club na Fealsúnachta works: what happens at a session, how to come along, RSVPs, membership, and how topics are chosen."
>
  <section class="cnf-section">
    <h1>{pageTitle}</h1>
    <div class="cnf-how">
      <p>
        New to the club? Here's what happens at a session and how to come along
        to your first one.
      </p>

    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="cnf-section">
    <div class="cnf-how">
      <h2>At a session</h2>
      <p>
        Each session is built around a question or a theme. There are no
        lectures and no right answers. We share our take, listen, and challenge
        each other's views, all in good spirits.
      </p>
      <p>
        A facilitator guides the discussion and keeps it moving, while the
        group decides where it goes. If there's a smaller crowd, we usually stay
        as one group. If there's a big crowd, we split into small groups, each
        with its own facilitator. Members are encouraged to have a go at
        facilitating. Every now and again we mix up the format too, to keep
        things fresh.
      </p>
      <p>
        Sessions run for about an hour and a half, in English, and you don't
        need any philosophy background. Afterwards, we head out for food and
        drinks, and the chat carries on.
      </p>

    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="cnf-section">
    <div class="cnf-how">
      <h2>Coming along</h2>
      <p>
        The club meets in chapters, each one a group in its own city, plus an
        Online chapter you can join from anywhere. Pick <a href="/chapters/"
          >your chapter</a
        > to see when and where it meets, and check its events for the next topic.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>In person:</strong> just turn up at the venue at the time on the
          event page.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Online:</strong> use the join button on the upcoming event's page
          when it's time.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        You can also subscribe to a chapter's calendar from its events page, so
        new sessions appear in your own calendar.
      </p>

    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="cnf-section">
    <div class="cnf-how">
      <h2>Common questions</h2>
      <div class="cnf-how__faq">
        <details class="cnf-how__question">
          <summary>Is it free?</summary>
          <p>
            Yes, sessions and membership are both free. If you'd like to support
            the club, you can <a href={DONATE_URL} target="_blank"
              >donate</a
            >.
          </p>
        </details>

        <details class="cnf-how__question">
          <summary>Do I need to be a member?</summary>
          <p>
            No, anyone can come along. A free account lets you RSVP to events,
            join your chapter for its news, and have a profile on the site.
          </p>
        </details>

        <details class="cnf-how__question" id="rsvp">
          <summary>Do I need to RSVP?</summary>
          <p>
            It's not required, but it helps. An RSVP on the event page gives us a
            headcount, which is handy when space is tight. You'll need a free
            account to RSVP.
          </p>
        </details>

        <details class="cnf-how__question">
          <summary>Do I have to speak?</summary>
          <p>
            Not at all. You're welcome to just listen, especially at your first
            session. Everyone joins in at their own pace, and no one will put you
            on the spot.
          </p>
        </details>

        <details class="cnf-how__question">
          <summary>Do I need to prepare anything?</summary>
          <p>
            No, just bring yourself and your curiosity. The topic's up on the
            event page beforehand if you want to mull it over, but there's no
            reading or homework.
          </p>
        </details>

        <details class="cnf-how__question">
          <summary>What language are sessions in?</summary>
          <p>
            English. Plenty of us aren't native speakers, so nobody minds if you
            take your time finding the words. Ideas matter more than perfect
            grammar.
          </p>
        </details>

        <details class="cnf-how__question">
          <summary>Can I bring a friend?</summary>
          <p>
            Absolutely, the more the merrier. They don't need an account to come
            along.
          </p>
        </details>

        <details class="cnf-how__question">
          <summary>How are topics chosen?</summary>
          <p>
            The organisers pick them, often following on from the last session
            or as part of a wider theme over a few weeks. Anyone can <a
              href="/suggest-topic/">suggest a topic</a
            >, and we draw on suggestions when choosing what's next.
          </p>
        </details>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
